---
description: Git workflow — land on main through PRs with Sonar green
alwaysApply: true
---

- **Do not push commits directly to `main`.** Direct pushes skip pull-request checks and are how Sonar went red on `main` (polyglot CI, PR #121).
- Work on a `cursor/...` branch, open a PR, and merge only when **SonarCloud Code Analysis** is green. Vercel still deploys from `main` after the merge.
- Before merge run `gh pr checks <n>` (or `npm run sonar:gate -- --status --pr <n>`). If Sonar is `fail` or pending, **stop**.
- Hot-fix on `main` only when the user explicitly asks **and** `npm run sonar:gate -- --status --branch main` is already OK.
- See `.cursor/rules/merge-quality-gate.mdc`.
